{"status":"ready","content":"I need to divide 123456789012345 by 98765.\n\nLet me work through this step by step.\n\nFirst, let me estimate the quotient: 123456789012345 ÷ 98765 ≈ 123456789012345 ÷ 100000 ≈ 1,234,567,890\n\nLet me be more precise. I'll compute 98765 × 1,249,857,381 and see how close we get.\n\nLet me try a systematic approach:\n\n98765 × 1,000,000,000 = 98,765,000,000,000\nRemainder: 123,456,789,012,345 - 98,765,000,000,000 = 24,691,789,012,345\n\n98765 × 200,000,000 = 19,753,000,000,000\nRemainder: 24,691,789,012,345 - 19,753,000,000,000 = 4,938,789,012,345\n\n98765 × 50,000,000 = 4,938,250,000,000\nRemainder: 4,938,789,012,345 - 4,938,250,000,000 = 539,012,345\n\n98765 × 5,000 = 493,825,000\nRemainder: 539,012,345 - 493,825,000 = 45,187,345\n\n98765 × 400 = 39,506,000\nRemainder: 45,187,345 - 39,506,000 = 5,681,345\n\n98765 × 57 = 5,629,605\nRemainder: 5,681,345 - 5,629,605 = 51,740\n\nSo the quotient is 1,000,000,000 + 200,000,000 + 50,000,000 + 5,000 + 400 + 57 = 1,250,005,457\n\nLet me verify: 98765 × 57 = 98765 × 50 + 98765 × 7 = 4,938,250 + 691,355 = 5,629,605 ✓\n\nCheck remainder: 51,740 < 98,765 ✓\n\nLet me verify by computing 98765 × 1,250,005,457:\n\n98765 × 1,250,005,457 = 98765 × 1,250,000,000 + 98765 × 5,457\n\n98765 × 1,250,000,000 = 98765 × 1,000,000,000 + 98765 × 250,000,000\n= 98,765,000,000,000 + 24,691,250,000,000 = 123,456,250,000,000\n\n98765 × 5,457 = 98765 × 5000 + 98765 × 457\n= 493,825,000 + 98765 × 457\n\n98765 × 457 = 98765 × 400 + 98765 × 57 = 39,506,000 + 5,629,605 = 45,135,605\n\n98765 × 5,457 = 493,825,000 + 45,135,605 = 538,960,605\n\nTotal: 123,456,250,000,000 + 538,960,605 = 123,456,788,960,605\n\nRemainder: 123,456,789,012,345 - 123,456,788,960,605 = 51,740\n\n**Quotient: 1,250,005,457**\n**Remainder: 51,740**\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Opus 4.6","modelId":"anthropic/claude-opus-4.6","promptId":"large-division","content":"I need to divide 123456789012345 by 98765.\n\nLet me work through this step by step.